Chapter: ProbeTailLoop

 Finding 33: bare metal tracks tail position and a self tail call there is
 a jump, so a `*-loop (xs) (i) (acc)` costs no stack; the zig plug called
 instead, and a Debug frame per element is a stack no thread has.

 Each definition here is a self tail call in one of the spine shapes the
 emitter now walks, and each is driven deep enough that a per-frame arm
 would be visibly different in cost while still finishing on both arms --
 the probe is about the ANSWER, and depth is what makes the answer
 evidence about frames rather than about arithmetic.

   count-if     the tail call sits under `if`
   count-let    a `let` binding stands between the if and the call
   count-match  the call sits in a `when` arm, which is tokenize-collect's
                own shape: if -> when -> if -> self call
   sum-nontail  NOT a tail call -- it must keep its frames and its answer,
                because an emitter that loops this one is wrong

 Expected on bare metal:

   count-if 200000
   count-let 200000
   count-match 200000
   sum-nontail 500500

Section: Shapes

  count-if : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-if (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else count-if (n - 1) (acc + 1)

  count-let : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-let (n) (acc) =
   if n == 0 then acc
   else let step = 1
   in count-let (n - 1) (acc + step)

  Step =
   | Stop
   | Go (Integer)

  next-step : Integer -> Step
  next-step (n) = if n == 0 then Stop else Go (n - 1)

  count-match : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-match (n) (acc) =
   when next-step n
    is Stop -> acc
    is Go (m) -> count-match m (acc + 1)

  sum-nontail : Integer -> Integer
  sum-nontail (n) =
   if n == 0 then 0
   else n + sum-nontail (n - 1)

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("count-if " & show (count-if 200000 0))
    print-line-uni ("count-let " & show (count-let 200000 0))
    print-line-uni ("count-match " & show (count-match 200000 0))
    print-line-uni ("sum-nontail " & show (sum-nontail 1000))
  end
